Apple operates a prepaid mail-in repair system using courier partnerships (FedEx) for device pickup and return, offering Express Replacement options alongside standard repair. Customers receive prepaid shipping labels, packaging, and estimated 7-14 day turnarounds. By managing reverse logistics directly, Apple controls quality, data security, and refurbishment pathways while reducing customer friction. This pick-up-at-home model democratizes access to manufacturer repair, preventing disposal of out-of-warranty devices.